Keep a shared rules as an empty list of text.
Place "a==b" into rules.
Place "b!=c" into rules.
Place "c==a" into rules.
Keep a shared parent as an empty list of whole numbers.
For every slot from 0 to 25, Place slot into parent.
Keep a shared alphabet as empty text.
Place "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz" into alphabet.
Keep a shared letter as empty text.
Keep a shared leftpairs as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared rightpairs as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared slot as 0.
Keep a shared ancestor as 0.
Keep a shared valid as 0.
Set valid to 1.

To locate.
Set slot to 0.
The current is slot.
Repeat while current is less than 26.
The symbol is the slice of alphabet from current to current plus 1.
If symbol matches letter, set slot to current, stop.
Add 1 to current.

To find from place (a whole number).
Set ancestor to place.
The current is ancestor.
Repeat while item current of parent is not current.
The next is item current of parent.
Set current to next.
Set ancestor to next.

To connect from first (a whole number) with second (a whole number).
Find from first.
The leftroot is ancestor.
Find from second.
The rightroot is ancestor.
If leftroot is not rightroot, set item leftroot of parent to rightroot.

To check from first (a whole number) with second (a whole number).
Find from first.
The leftroot is ancestor.
Find from second.
The rightroot is ancestor.
If leftroot is rightroot, set valid to 0.

For each rule in rules.
The leftletter is the slice of rule from 0 to 1.
The mark is the slice of rule from 1 to 2.
The rightletter is the slice of rule from 3 to 4.
Set letter to leftletter.
Locate.
The leftslot is slot.
Set letter to rightletter.
Locate.
The rightslot is slot.
If mark matches "=", connect from leftslot with rightslot, otherwise Place leftslot into leftpairs, Place rightslot into rightpairs.

For every which from 0 to the last position of leftpairs.
The one is item which of leftpairs.
The two is item which of rightpairs.
Check from one with two.

If valid is 1, show true, otherwise show false.
